day in October","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:42","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Administrative divisions","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:43","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:44","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Constitution Day, 30 August (1976)","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:45","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"Turks and Caicos Islands Constitution Order 2006 (effective 9 August 2006)","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:46","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"based on laws of England and Wales, with a few adopted from Jamaica and The Bahamas","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:47","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"18 years of age; universal","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:48","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: Queen ELIZABETH II (since 6 February 1952); represented by Governor Richard TAUWHARE (since 11 July 2005)\n\nhead of government: Premier Michael Eugene MISICK (since 15 August 2003); note - the office of premier was created in the 2006 constitution\n\ncabinet: Cabinet consists of the governor, the premier, six ministers appointed by the governor from among the members of the House of Assembly, and the attorney general\n\nelections: none; the monarch is hereditary; governor appointed by the monarch; following legislative elections, the leader of the majority party is appointed premier by the governor","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:49","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral House of Assembly (21 seats of which 15 are popularly elected; members serve four-year terms)\n\nelections: last held 9 February 2007 (next to be held in 2011)\n\nelection results: percent of vote by party - PNP 60%, PDM 40%; seats by party - PNP 13, PDM 2","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:50","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"Supreme Court; Court of Appeal","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:51","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"People's Democratic Movement or PDM [Floyd SEYMOUR]; Progressive National Party or PNP [Michael Eugene MISICK]","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:52","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"NA","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:53","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"Caricom (associate), CDB, Interpol (subbureau), UPU","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:54","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:55","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (overseas territory of the UK)","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:56","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"blue, with the flag of the UK in the upper hoist-side quadrant and the colonial shield centered on the outer half of the flag; the shield is yellow and contains a conch shell, lobster, and cactus","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:57","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"The Turks and Caicos economy is based on tourism, offshore financial services, and fishing. Most capital goods and food for domestic consumption are imported. The US is the leading source of tourists, accounting for more than three-quarters of the 175,000 visitors that arrived in 2004. Major sources of government revenue also include fees from offshore financial activities and customs receipts.","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:58","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$216 million (2002 est.)","ordinal":59,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:59","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (official exchange rate)","content":"$NA","ordinal":60,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:60","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - real growth rate","content":"4.9% (2000 est.)","ordinal":61,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:61","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - per capita (PPP)","content":"$11,500 (2002 est.)","ordinal":62,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:62","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP - composition by sector","content":"agriculture: NA%\n\nindustry: NA%\n\nservices: NA%","ordinal":63,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:63","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force","content":"4,848 (1990 est.)","ordinal":64,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/tk.html#field:64","country":"TC","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Labor force - by occu